## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical mastery of tenant isolation, cross-account access, and automated containment in AWS, plus how to validate security controls under real-world pressures.

## Key Concepts

- ABAC with aws:PrincipalTag for tenant-scoped access
- S3 Access Points and per-tenant prefixes for isolation
- Tenant-scoped KMS keys with rotation
- EventBridge + Lambda + Step Functions for rapid containment
- Immutable audit trails with CloudTrail and S3 Object Lock

## Code Example

```javascript
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:ListBucket","s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket-${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}",
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket-${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- What signals would trigger the containment workflow and how would you test them?
- How would you validate that rotation and ABAC policies cannot be bypassed during an incident?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests fundamental cross-account trust, basic least privilege, and incident containment at beginner level.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account IAM role and trust relationships
- S3 bucket policy and KMS encryption, per-tenant CMK
- Credential rotation and rapid containment

## Code Example
```json
// Trust policy snippet (tenant account -> analytics role)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ANALYTICS_ACCOUNT_ID:role/TenantAnalyticsRole"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"sts:ExternalId": "tenant-123-ext"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
// Per-tenant bucket access policy (simplified)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-123-data/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:SourceArn": "arn:aws:iam::ANALYTICS_ACCOUNT_ID:user/tenant-123"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to handle 2+ tenants with minimal policy duplication?
- What monitoring would you add to detect misconfigurations or breaches?
